Copyleft (LGPL) components embedded in the compiled binaries via the Bun runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Bun runtime (MIT, https://github.com/oven-sh/bun) statically links several
components that are covered by copyleft licenses. Because the Xata CLI embeds the
Bun runtime, these components are present in the Xata CLI executables.

JavaScriptCore / WebKit (and WebCore)
  License:  LGPL-2.1 (with portions under BSD-2-Clause / BSD-3-Clause)
  How it is included:  Bun uses JavaScriptCore as its JavaScript engine and
    STATICALLY LINKS it (and WebCore). When the Xata CLI is compiled with
    `bun build --compile`, the resulting executable contains the Bun runtime
    and, with it, JavaScriptCore/WebKit. No Xata proprietary code is linked into
    JavaScriptCore; it is combined only as part of the Bun runtime, unmodified.
  Corresponding source:  Bun builds against its own WebKit fork, which is the
    corresponding source for the version shipped:
      https://github.com/oven-sh/webkit
    Bun pins the exact WebKit revision it builds against for each Bun release;
    the Bun version embedded in a given Xata CLI release is recorded in that
    release (see `xata version` and the release manifest). Upstream WebKit is at
    https://webkit.org and https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit.

tinycc (TinyCC)
  License:  LGPL-2.1
  How it is included:  Statically linked by the Bun runtime.
  Source:  https://github.com/oven-sh/tinycc (Bun fork) / https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git

